Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Booleans: the decomposition of a walking intersection line at the faces'
boundaries reads no point past the line's ends (mitcad#1819).

IntTools_WLineTool::DecompositionOfWLine, where it moves a sub-line's end
point onto a natural boundary or near a tangent zone, looks along the line
for a neighbouring point distinct from the end's neighbour: two loops step
the index one point on and read theWLine->Point(index) before the loop's
condition checks it, so where every point up to the line's end lies on
the neighbour (within gp::Resolution) the last step reads Point(0) or
Point(NbPnts + 1). A release build has no range check there and read a
null node (a segmentation fault: a boolean of a two-distance chamfer of a
tangent chain over a cylinder strip with the body it was made on); a
debug build raised Standard_OutOfRange. Each loop now stops before an
index outside 1..NbPnts, as when it finds no distinct point; every case
that read only points of the line keeps its result.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1695.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_WLineTool.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_WLineTool.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_WLineTool.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_WLineTool.cxx
@@ -853,6 +853,11 @@
               while ((anindexother <= iLast) && (anindexother >= iFirst))
               {
                 anindexother = (j == 0) ? (anindexother + 1) : (anindexother - 1);
+                if (anindexother < 1 || anindexother > aNbPnts)
+                {
+                  // Past the line's end: no point there to compare with.
+                  break;
+                }
                 const IntSurf_PntOn2S& aPrevNeighbourPoint = theWLine->Point(anindexother);
                 double                 nU2, nV2;
 
@@ -984,6 +989,11 @@
             {
               aneighbourpointindex2 =
                 (j == 0) ? (aneighbourpointindex2 + 1) : (aneighbourpointindex2 - 1);
+              if (aneighbourpointindex2 < 1 || aneighbourpointindex2 > aNbPnts)
+              {
+                // Past the line's end: no point there to compare with.
+                break;
+              }
               const IntSurf_PntOn2S& aPrevNeighbourPoint = theWLine->Point(aneighbourpointindex2);
               double                 nU2, nV2;
 
